WEBVTT

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.390
Good work, Rin.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.440
Are you okay, Rina-san?

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:33.860
That was a close one.
It almost took Momo-chan away.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:35.990
We would've been just one again.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.330
The red fog is
the thickest it's ever been.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.330
The bugs are really strong too.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.540
Yeah, even though we're staying away
from the red root.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.340
This sure is tough.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.720
Rin, don't worry. Let's keep at it.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.430
Yeah, let's go.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.650
If you're going to sit around,
Rina-chan's going to eat them all.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.240
Thanks.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:19.410
Let's just stay away from the root
and go where the fog is light.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:23.620
Wakaba-kun, can you tell
where the nearest root is?

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.380
This side feels a bit warm.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.550
We may be too close.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.430
Then let's follow it
while keeping our distance.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:42.010
It branches off here and there,
so we'll have to cross it sometimes.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.930
Is Wakaba really right?

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
Can you see it too, Sis Rin?

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.600
Yeah, I see a red light sometimes.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.200
Oh, look!

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:02.530
Hey, it's the white one.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.170
You're alive! How've you been?

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.710
I'm surprised it isn't a Red Bug yet.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.300
It's so smart.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:17.260
Wakaba, Rinaji is smarter!

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:20.760
Hey, we don't have time for that.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.970
I BROUGHT MAP.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.480
"I brought map."

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.690
Wait, is this a map of Island Eight?

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.690
We're around here now, so...

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:44.280
if we go here, we can avoid the roots
and reach Island Nine.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.660
This is amazing, white one!

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.080
Can we trust it?

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:51.040
Hold on a second.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.010
It's exactly the same. It seems reliable.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.600
Let's go then.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:11.940
Inside the dark my heartbeat echoes

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:18.820
Long night will continue on

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:22.410
Time to face the hell that surrounds you
Before you crash and burn

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.780
Within the fire
Your soul will rise now

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:45.220
Breathe in, breathe out
Your blank gaze on the brink of life

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:52.020
Step hard on the accelerator now
Escape the tunnel and overtake that pain

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:59.030
A shadow disappears into smoke

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:06.870
Lost light will continue on tomorrow

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:14.000
Someday our world will change
Inside a fantasy Remember, remember

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:21.090
I will mercilessly break your dream
and steal it away, with these hands

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:27.470
Until this body breaks
Beyond the limit We'll never surrender

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.850
Endless agony

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.150
Finding my life in the KEMURIKUSA

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:05.430
If this is the right path, we can
avoid the root and reach the trunk.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:06.930
No red fog, either.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.100
Good work, white one.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:15.020
I never would've guessed we'd get
this map. What a great help.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:19.400
HELP WAKABA. LIKE.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.240
You're so nice.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.280
-Maybe more useful than Wakaba.
-Yeah.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.450
What?

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.530
Let's go this way for now.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:44.050
These are so easy to grab onto.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.180
And no red fog.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.430
This is great.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.020
Why is it still following us?

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:01.690
Seems like it's following Wakaba-kun.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.950
WAKABA, NEED HELP?

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.450
Not for now.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:12.700
What? You can tell what it's saying?

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:14.370
That's not fair!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.960
WAKABA, OTHER NAMES?

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:21.210
Oh, the others' names? Okay then.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.920
Ritsu-san, Rin-san.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.420
And these are the Rina-sans.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:30.760
Rinayo-san, Rinacchi-san,
Rinaji-san, and Rinamu-san.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:32.550
Huh?

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.470
You can tell us apart?

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.980
Yes, of course I can.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.230
Don't get cheeky with us!

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:48.240
"Ritsu. Rinas."

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:50.660
"Rin." Right!

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.410
Another weird thing.

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:57.160
Don't get distracted.
Exterminate it if it gets in the way.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.210
"Rin is obstinate."

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:04.960
No, wasn't me! I didn't say that!

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:15.470
This path is bug-free
and so easy to pass through.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:19.640
Let's let Rina-chan and Wakaba-kun
rest for a while.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:20.850
Sure.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:32.360
Let me see...okay.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:39.500
THE WALL IS PROBABLY KEMURIKUSA TOO.
EVEN RIKU CAN'T CONTROL IT.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:45.790
THE SMOKE'S ORDERS MAKE THE BUGS MOVE?
THE RED KEMURIKUSA?

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:51.630
I'M CURIOUS ABOUT THE ISLANDS' TERRAIN.
DID THEY MOVE? THE JOINTS ARE WEIRD.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:56.850
THE FIRST PERSON'S LEAF IS THE MEMORY
LEAF? CAN'T OPEN IT. RYO HAS IT RIGHT NOW.

00:07:57.010 --> 00:08:03.560
EYES, EARS, NOSE, TONGUE. RIKU IS SKIN?
RIN IS THE BODY? STRENGTH?

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:06.860
Really? Rin-san?

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:08.570
What?

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:13.990
Do you sense any red roots around here?

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:19.740
Oh, yes. The roots. Okay, one second.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.210
What's with you?

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:30.880
It's still a ways away.

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:34.590
But there's a medium-sized one
in the way we're headed.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:35.970
Okay.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.180
We'll have to fight when we near it.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.520
Drink up while you can.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:45.270
Oh, thank you.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:48.480
You should get some rest too.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.940
Do you want some water?

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.740
I'm still fine.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.990
Give some to the Rinas later.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:59.740
But don't wake them up yet.
Let them sleep while they can.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:03.250
You're so nice, Rin-san.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:05.620
This journey was my decision.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:09.130
I want to make it
as safe as possible for them.

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:14.170
Rin-san, that leaf...

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:19.100
That's a Kemurikusa too, right?

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:22.810
Yeah, but I've never been able to use it.

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:26.850
Is that the First Person's leaf?

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:29.440
How did you know...? That's right.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:33.690
Can I touch that a little?

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.650
Huh? What do you mean?

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:39.870
Stop your nonsense.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:45.660
Oh, I just thought it might have some
important information or something...

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:50.420
Are we close?

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:54.130
Yeah, I hear something too.

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:03.930
Ouch!

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:11.310
The map says there should be a path here.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.190
It's collapsed.

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:18.320
I think there might be
a red root past here.

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.490
Then we have to go around it anyways.

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:23.990
Maybe that way?

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:34.250
Seems like that's the only way out.

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.010
Let's follow it.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:03.910
Wow, what a place! It's so interesting!

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:07.790
-It's huge!
-Rina's never eaten it before.

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:09.330
Rina, be careful.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:13.670
It's warm.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:17.510
That must be the one I've been feeling.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:23.470
The red fog is too thick in the valley
to get to the trunk.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:27.270
Even if we got across,
there're a lot of roots on the mountain.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:31.520
Aren't there any more tunnels?

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:33.100
Yeah, on the other side.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:36.190
You don't have a map
past this point, do you?

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:40.320
WOULD MAP HELP?

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:42.240
You have one?

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:56.750
-Where's it going?
-Yeah.

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:02.880
What the...

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.210
Whoa, that scared me!

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:35.670
-What is this?
-Huh?

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:44.470
Why...?

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:48.430
THEY LISTEN TO NUSHI.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:50.430
What's going on?

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.180
Who are they?

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:55.350
HAVE A SEAT.

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.730
What now?

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:03.700
What is this place?

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:06.860
HERE? INSIDE BOAT.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:09.740
THIS PLACE, OUR AREA.

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:14.870
White one, you mean
these other ones are saying that?

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:17.920
What have they been doing here?

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.090
"Sleeping"?

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:25.590
"Red roots all over."

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:31.640
"Red root, red smoke, dangerous."

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:36.020
"Crossed mountain from other side."

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.770
Does it mean Island Nine?

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:42.900
"Captain, gone."

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:45.700
"No more job."

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:49.990
"City, sinking."

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:54.700
"Low place, red smoke, dangerous."

00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:00.130
So they've escaped here
from the other side.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:01.880
The opposite of us.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:04.550
Guess we've all been through a lot.

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:07.800
We have no time for these bugs.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:10.470
Let's think of a way to go forward.

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.680
"That's obstinate."

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:16.520
No, that wasn't me!

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:21.810
If it's from Island Nine,
maybe it can tell us something.

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.570
"That's smart."

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.990
Right?

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:29.490
Gotta hand it to Rinaji.

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:34.370
Can you tell us something
about Island Nine?

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:39.120
"Wall was made. So don't know anymore."

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.250
"Can't go back."

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:47.670
"Wall, blue smoke, dangerous."

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:49.840
"Turns us blue."

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:55.810
"We like Captain's orders
more than smoke's orders."

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.140
"We live for Captain's orders."

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:02.900
"Be our Captain."

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:05.650
What, huh? Me?

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:11.280
GIVE US ORDER. WE'LL DO ANYTHING.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:12.910
Yes, well...

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:16.580
For now, we want a map.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:19.790
MAP!

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:22.040
THERE'S MAP FROM OTHER SIDE OF MOUNTAIN.

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.790
GIVE THEM MAP.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:35.640
Huh?

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:43.560
GOT MAP. WANT TO SEE?

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:47.610
A map to get to Island Nine?

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:52.110
Look, there might be a tunnel
on that side too.

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:58.870
But we'll have to cross that red root.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:03.790
You're right. Either we go unnoticed
or we destroy it.

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:12.430
Huh? Rin-san, look.

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:14.720
It's crumbled a bit.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:23.440
That structure is deteriorating
due to the red fog.

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:25.150
Be careful.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:29.070
Could we move the root if we destroy it?

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:30.530
That's a good idea.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:35.410
I'll go then. It's in the red fog.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:39.660
Rin, that's too dangerous.
Let's think of another way.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:45.170
If the root notices us before we reach it,
it'll spout tons of red bugs.

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:50.460
CAPTAIN WAKABA.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:52.340
THEY WANT TO HELP CAPTAIN.

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:18.280
CUT RED ROOT HELPFUL?

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.750
Yeah, that'd be a huge help!

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:38.930
There's no reaction.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:42.810
Maybe that root reacts to Kemurikusa too.

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:49.360
CAPTAIN, GIVE US PERMISSION.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:54.650
Permission? Do I touch you?

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:26.980
-They reached it!
-Oh, wow!

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:01.390
I have to save them!

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:06.850
DON'T WORRY. THEY DO TILL END.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:29.210
Are you all okay?

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:44.600
"Pretty much okay."

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:49.310
"Red smoke, dangerous."

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:52.020
"Will stop functioning."

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:54.310
What now?

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:58.730
They're going to stop functioning
before they turn into Red Bugs.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:05.240
That's it! Maybe I can neutralize it
with Midori-san.

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:10.620
Their main body leaves are almost gone.

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.670
It's the end for them.

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:18.630
"Captain, thank you
for giving us purpose."

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:23.090
"Thank you for
letting us do what we like."

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:36.190
It's my fault...

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:38.650
Because I told them to...

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:47.660
WHY CRY? THEY WERE GRATEFUL.

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:55.290
I understand a little bit
how you feel now.

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:02.800
Both my sisters were smiling in the end.

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:08.390
I'm sure those bugs were glad
they met you before the end.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:19.690
I'm fine now. Let's go.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:27.240
Would you cry if we died too?

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:30.910
Of course I would!

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:34.040
I won't ever let that happen!

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:34.620
I don't want anyone else dying either.

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:36.870
I won't let it happen.

00:23:39.710 --> 00:23:41.290
You included.
